WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:01.429
Speaker 6: Are people actually doing that?

00:00:01.429 --> 00:00:04.370
Because from conservatives, I hear all the
time that, like, people don't want to work

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:21.740
and they'll just, you know, apply to a job
just to get unemployment.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:31.630
And one note, that's actually a thing that
happens.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:48.430
Speaker 1: So first of all, in order to initially
qualify for unemployment, you actually have

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.000
to be unemployed.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.520
So in normal circumstances, you have to have
lost a job but not been fired for cause.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:00:59.520
Right.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:07.010
And so first, so just to qualify for unemployment,
some some barriers have to be some threshold

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.210
has to be met.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:28.340
Is it as simple as applying to a few jobs
to continue receiving unemployment?

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.189
It basically is, yeah.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.189
And it depends on the state.

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:37.440
Like, for example, when I was in college,
I used to work for the now defunct Circuit

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.820
City, and when they switched from commission
to hourly for salespeople, they laid off the

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.010
top salespeople, one of which I was.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:48.380
And so I got to collect unemployment because
my my position was eliminated.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.610
I had to go on and say, I'm looking for a
job.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.880
I wasn't asked where did I apply?

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.720
It was just how have you been looking for
a job?

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.720
Yes, I have.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.369
And then I would get the money.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:03.040
That system may have changed.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.350
The systems are different in each state.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.939
That is something that you can do.

00:02:11.939 --> 00:02:16.349
You apply for a few jobs and then you continue
collecting unemployment.

00:02:16.349 --> 00:02:22.069
I am not worried about this and I've made
a couple of clips explaining why.

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:25.590
But fundamentally enhanced unemployment ends
in September.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:30.180
You are not allowed to be on unemployment
an indefinite amount of time.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:37.590
Many people, many, many people in the fall
are going to get to the end of unemployment.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.669
And at that point, they are going to stop
receiving the benefits.

00:02:40.669 --> 00:02:53.409
So they are either going to have to figure
out how to pay for their expenses without

00:02:53.409 --> 00:03:04.720
making any money or they're going to have
to go and get themselves a job.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.919
So any any social insurance program will have
some free riders or people who just do the

00:03:08.919 --> 00:03:15.999
minimum in order to keep collecting the unemployment
as long as the system big picture is working

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:25.329
and unemployment and enhanced unemployment
saved so many people during the pandemic,

00:03:25.329 --> 00:03:40.940
I don't worry about a few free riders.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.219
They're going to lose their benefits relatively
soon anyway.

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:46.229
The benefits don't last forever.

00:03:46.229 --> 00:03:52.541
Speaker 6: I think you suggest if a conservative
is saying that, like, you know, unemployment

00:03:52.541 --> 00:03:58.959
is just keeping people lazy and keeping lost
and working, just like just like you mentioned

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:04.010
the benefits and say that like it's not actually,
as you know, reliable to like liberals, as

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.119
conservatives think it is.

00:04:05.119 --> 00:04:06.119
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:04:06.119 --> 00:04:11.069
And there is no evidence that most people
want to earn what you learn on unemployment

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:12.069
and don't work.

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:19.600
We have a really rare situation right now
because of the pandemic and the enhanced unemployment.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.919
But generally speaking, people want to work.

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:23.240
Generally speaking, you make more working
than on state unemployment.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.889
Now, we have a again, we have an enhanced
unemployment and there are some people who

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:28.060
would be satisfied just making unemployment
and and not working.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.280
But it's very few many people get meaning
from work.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.669
People get a connection to other people.

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:34.550
Most people want to work, period.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:35.550
Speaker 6: Right.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.300
This is actually my first time trying to call
it so it means a lot to be able to speak with

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.300
you.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.300
So beautiful for all the content.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.300
Speaker 1: Thanks for the call.

